# Files whose bytes are checked against a recorded hash, or against the blob
# git holds, must not be rewritten on checkout. With `core.autocrlf=true` -
# the Git for Windows default - they were checked out with CRLF line endings,
# and `audit/vitals.py` then refused its own vendored web-vitals build
# ("artifact hash differs from its manifest"), which took the whole browser
# pass down on Windows.
audit/vendor/** -text
validation/assets/** -text
